| 🧩 **Testing Type**        | 🎯 **Why We Need It**                                        | 🧠 **Purpose**                                                         | 💎 **Advantages**                                           | 🌍 **Real-Time Example**                                                                         |
| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| 🧪 **Smoke Testing**       | ✅ To quickly ensure **basic APIs** work after deployment.    | 🔍 Validate if main endpoints respond correctly before deeper testing. | ⏱️ Saves time by catching **major issues early**.           | 💳 After deploying a payment API, check if `/login`, `/pay`, and `/status` respond successfully. |
| ⚙️ **Functional Testing**  | ✔️ To verify the API meets **business requirements**.        | 🧩 Compare actual vs. expected results from endpoints.                 | 🎯 Ensures **accuracy and reliability** of API logic.       | 📊 Testing if `/calculateTax?amount=1000` returns the correct tax as per rules.                  |
| 🔗 **Integration Testing** | 🔄 To ensure **multiple APIs** work together smoothly.       | 🧵 Test **data flow and communication** between services.              | 🧠 Detects issues in **end-to-end workflows**.              | 👥 Checking if `/login` connects correctly with `/getUserProfile` and `/getUserOrders`.          |
| 🔁 **Regression Testing**  | ♻️ To confirm new updates **don’t break** existing features. | 🔁 Re-run older test cases after changes or fixes.                     | 💪 Maintains **stability and consistency**.                 | 🛍️ After adding discounts, ensure `/orderSummary` still returns correct totals.                 |
| 📈 **Load Testing**        | 🚀 To assess **performance under normal loads**.             | 👥 Simulate concurrent users calling APIs.                             | ⚡ Identifies **bottlenecks** and ensures scalability.       | 🧮 Simulating 1000 users calling `/searchProducts` simultaneously.                               |
| 💥 **Stress Testing**      | 🔥 To test **extreme or unexpected loads**.                  | 💣 Push system beyond its limits intentionally.                        | 🧱 Reveals breaking points and **improves robustness**.     | 🛒 Sending 10,000 `/checkout` requests to test system limits during a flash sale.                |
| 🔐 **Security Testing**    | 🛡️ To prevent **unauthorized access** or **data leaks**.    | 🕵️ Check for vulnerabilities and weak spots.                          | 🔒 Ensures **data protection** and compliance (e.g., GDPR). | 🚫 Trying SQL injection on `/getUserData` to verify sensitive info isn’t exposed.                |
| 💻 **UI Testing**          | 🖥️ To confirm **data from APIs** displays correctly in UI.  | 🔄 Verify UI and API integration accuracy.                             | 🌟 Ensures a **consistent user experience**.                | 🧾 Checking if `/getProductDetails` data appears properly on product page.                       |
| 🧨 **Fuzz Testing**        | 🎲 To find **hidden bugs** via invalid or random inputs.     | 🧬 Inject unexpected data to test API behavior.                        | 🧩 Improves **stability** and prevents crashes.             | 🧠 Sending malformed JSON to `/submitFeedback` to test error handling.                           |
